{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 17384018383796506621, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 663, "mtime": 1791871763.458701, "sha256": "6660c9b25e6c90cd4bd5df37698a644a54b84dc37582a472153798eed7440bcf"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 426, "mtime": 1791871767.351058, "sha256": "a6af430231c707ec4904188141885c0e1d4a6697098a28cc5988942c69cfe8ef"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/11/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/11/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test covering the reported case plus the half-even trap (`0.125`) and the negative case.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. I checked this with a direct script because pytest isn't installed here, so the new test file hasn't been run.\n\n**Cause:** there were two problems in `pricing/money.py`:\n- The float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round()` rounds it down.\n- `round()` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, not up. For example, `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`. So the \"half up\" promised in the docstring never happened.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the number to the decimal text it displays as (`str(x)`, so `\"2.675\"`) and rounds that with `Decimal.quantize(..., ROUND_HALF_UP)`. It still returns a `float`, so `add_vat` and other callers don't need changes. Negative values round away from zero: `-2.675` becomes `-2.68`.\n\n**Checked** (old `round` \u2192 new `round_money`):\n\n| input | old | new |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2.675 | 2.67 | 2.68 |\n| 0.125 | 0.12 | 0.13 |\n| 1.005 | 1.0 | 1.01 |\n| 2.674 | 2.67 | 2.67 |\n| -2.675 | -2.67 | -2.68 |\n\n`split(10.00, 3)` still gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`.\n\nI added `tests/test_round_money.py` with the same cases as a regression test.\n\n`split` is separate and I didn't change it: it uses `int(total * 100)`, which can cut off a cent when the float sits just below the true value.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 281976, "requests_cache_write": 10707, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1590982, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2454, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial11", "run_seed": 20